{%- comment -%}
  Fyxx: Brand line (product block)
  Part of the wine-template buy column, directly above the <h1>: uppercase,
  letter-spaced, bold and full ink, so it reads as the producer name rather than
  a faint eyebrow. No font-family is declared; it inherits the theme body font.

  Source. custom.brand is "#REF!" on most wines (a broken spreadsheet formula
  that got imported), so it cannot be trusted. Every wine instead carries a clean
  "Brand_<name>" tag, the live source, read the same way block.product-wine-meta
  reads Country_ and Region_. So:
    1. Find the first tag beginning "Brand_". Keep the raw tag (for the link) and
       the name with the prefix removed and trimmed (some tags have a leading
       space after the underscore, e.g. "Brand_ Machareus").
    2. Display name: use custom.brand when it is present and is not "#REF!",
       otherwise the name from the tag.
    3. Render nothing at all when there is neither.
    4. When a Brand_ tag exists, link the name to the "wine" collection filtered
       by that tag: {{ routes.collections_url }}/wine/{{ brand_tag | handleize }}.
       handleize of the raw tag is exactly what Shopify matches the product's own
       tag against, so accents, ampersands and apostrophes all resolve (verified
       live: Gato Negro, Gerard Bertrand, Moet & Chandon, Chateau d'Esclans).
       With no tag there is no link, just text.

  No JavaScript. The first Brand_ tag wins; a handful of wines carry two (the
  Domaine Derain wines), which is reported separately.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign brand_meta = product.metafields.custom.brand.value | default: ''
  if brand_meta == '#REF!'
    assign brand_meta = ''
  endif

  assign brand_tag = ''
  assign tag_name = ''
  for tag in product.tags
    assign t = tag | strip
    assign p6 = t | slice: 0, 6
    if p6 == 'Brand_'
      assign brand_tag = t
      assign tag_name = t | remove_first: 'Brand_' | strip
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign brand_name = brand_meta
  if brand_name == blank
    assign brand_name = tag_name
  endif
-%}

{%- if brand_name != blank -%}
  <div class="fx-brand" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- if brand_tag != blank -%}
      <p class="fx-brand__text"><a class="fx-brand__link" href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/wine/{{ brand_tag | handleize }}">{{ brand_name | escape }}</a></p>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="fx-brand__text">{{ brand_name | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <style>
    .fx-brand__text {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #100F0D;
    }
    .fx-brand__link {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .fx-brand__link:hover,
    .fx-brand__link:focus-visible {
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
